it('com BarcodeDetector no navegador, lê o QR da câmera ("enc_5e6f7a8b:K7M2QX") e registra a presença', async () => {
  const { falsa, api, window, container } = await montar()
  falsa.responde('POST /encontros/enc_5e6f7a8b/presencas', 201, {
    id: 'pre_3a4b5c6d', encontroId: 'enc_5e6f7a8b', participanteId: 'p-carla', origem: 'qr',
    lidoEm: '2026-10-19T19:10:00-03:00', registradaEm: '2026-10-19T19:10:00-03:00', justificativa: null
  })
  // BarcodeDetector falso: devolve uma leitura na primeira detecção e depois fica em espera
  let chamadas = 0
  window.BarcodeDetector = class {
    detect() {
      chamadas += 1
      if (chamadas === 1) return Promise.resolve([{ rawValue: 'enc_5e6f7a8b:K7M2QX' }])
      return new Promise(() => {})
    }
  }
  navigator.mediaDevices = { getUserMedia: () => Promise.resolve({}) }
  await render(container, { api, agora: () => '2026-10-19T19:10:00-03:00' })
  await pausa(); await pausa(); await pausa();

  const chamada = falsa.chamadas.find((c) => c.metodo === 'POST')
  assert.deepEqual(chamada.corpo, { codigo: 'K7M2QX' })
  assert.match(container.querySelector('.presenca').textContent, /origem qr/)
})
```

Note navigator.mediaDevices — in happy-dom, navigator may be read-only with mediaDevices possibly undefined. Setting `navigator.mediaDevices = {...}` in node/happy-dom should work since it's a plain object. But if happy-dom freezes navigator, assignment fails silently (non-strict) or throws (strict mode - modules are strict). Use try or Object.defineProperty. Let me instead set via defineProperty:

```js
Object.defineProperty(navigator, 'mediaDevices', { value: { getUserMedia: () => Promise.resolve({}) }, configurable: true })
```

Same for window.BarcodeDetector — window is a normal object; assignment fine.

Now implement iniciarScanner in the module and wire in render. The scanner needs aoLer function that parses "enc_...:codigo" and calls registrarLeitura with those values directly (bypassing select). Let me define in render:

```js
iniciarScanner((conteudo) => {
  const [encontroId, codigo] = String(conteudo).trim().split(':')
  if (!encontroId || !codigo) return
  registrarLeitura({ api, agora, areaResultado, areaFila, aoEnviarFila, encontroId, codigo })
})
```

iniciarScanner module function using window.BarcodeDetector + navigator.mediaDevices, video, detector.detect loop.

Important: after processing reading, the loop calls ler() again → second detect returns pending promise → test ends. Good. But there's a risk: with new window per test but module `filaAtual` global persists across tests — only matters for online listener; the scanner tests don't touch fila. Except registered listener guarded per window flag → in test 6 new window, flag false → registers another listener. Fine. But note `window.__m3FilaOnline` flag is on each new window so re-registration each test — good, since addEventListener is per-window too.

Wait — but the module `filaAtual` from a previous test could be triggered? No new 'online' dispatched in test 6.

